<!--
COLUMN GUIDANCE

Session date — the date the session ran. One row per session, not per stage.

Stage — the Appendix A stage number and name. If a session crossed a stage
boundary, say so explicitly: that usually means the gate was skipped, and it
is worth catching here rather than three stages later.

What shipped — concrete artifacts, not activity. "Matching engine + 41 unit
tests" rather than "worked on matching". Link commits where useful.

DoD criteria met — quote the stage's testable definition of done from Appendix
A and say which parts are green. PARTIAL IS A VALID ANSWER AND MUST BE SAID SO;
a row claiming a gate is met when it is not is the single most expensive lie
this file can carry, because the next session builds on it.

Next — the first thing the next session should do, specific enough to act on
without re-reading anything.
-->
